aren't there and then but they're still of that day of that site</p><p><strong>14:21</strong> but they're probably maybe 30 45 seconds long so we can use it in both formats but we can actually just take it online and offline or there and then or after the fact and that gives us the ability to use it in both ways and it actually does there's no difference in how the both of those approaches work in quickler because you might tell me different but quickler doesn't care if i do it there and then or quickler doesn't care if i do it after the fact what it cares about is the fact i've done it we're excited about what it's doing for our business because</p><p><strong>14:56</strong> it's doing something else as well one of the things we've done since seeing how it works for the auditing and reporting is we've actually put it to work solving another problem for our business which is the completion of cosh assessments or assessments for substances that need a chemical risk assessment things that are covered by the control of substances hazardous to health regulations and this is a really important but quite repetitious task that we have in our business we already have a software solution bundled as part of one of our other software</p><p><strong>15:32</strong> packages that will perform the function for us but it can take between 20 to 30 to minutes to do it and it is very clunky and it's not very user-friendly at all it is literally re-typing information that exists on a safety data sheet into something that is no more advanced than an online form and when we do that that's quite frustrating because we are you know well-paid reasonably intelligent consultants that are really just</p><p><strong>16:05</strong> you know re-typing documents for no other reason than there's no better way of doing it but when we put the task to you at quickler to solve what we end up with is the same approach as we use at site reporting and which has the ability to create a COSHH assessment in a tenth of the time and there's no re-typing of information and what we're doing for the sake of transparency is we're giving it the safety data sheet in a pdf format and then we the qualified consultants are actually filling in some details about how who where why and when subject the</p><p><strong>16:42</strong> substance is going to be used and those two things combined together are the quickler using the pdf of the safety data sheet and our consultant input which maybe only takes two minutes to give that input the record is 45 seconds well the record is 45 seconds and we probably don't want it to be any quicker than that but but because you know it's a really it's a higher hazard activity and it's something that we probably want to do with a degree of caution but when we do it we're actually producing something that's better than what we produced</p><p><strong>17:13</strong> before so there's a visible difference there from the the quickler reporting that we've seen on other other sectors but we've got a COSHH assessment in a tenth of the time and it is exactly the format that we wanted it to be because we're in control of that we authored that and we take pride in the quality of that document that we give to our customers but we've found that to be an absolute game changer because it was one of these tasks that was a very frustrating task within the business you know if you phoned today and said i need 10 COSHH assessments i'd be perfectly polite on the phone and i would say yeah that's absolutely</p><p><strong>17:48</strong> something that i can do for you but then when the phone went down inwardly i would think gee i've got to do 10 COSHH assessments and your heart would sink a small amount and you would think you know the first one or two obviously are quite interesting but then you've just got to do the same thing 10 times time but the frustration of having to spend 20 minutes retyping information from one format to another and we haven't seen anything that does it like quickler like i say we had access to something before that was systemized had a database of COSHH assessments sometimes it had the thing that you were looking for sometimes it didn't</p><p><strong>18:21</strong> and there's you know tens of thousands of individual compounds out there that need cautious and we really saw it as a solution for that problem that we didn't see when we first engaged with quickler so when we first took on the kosh task it came out of a conversation in our office where somebody says well if it does this can it do that and i think that's probably what our thinking is going to be when a task like that presents itself now is can quickler do it and the answer is maybe but in reality if quickler can do it it can do it in</p><p><strong>18:55</strong> a way that is so efficient that we don't have to spend a huge amount of our own time actually doing the administrative part of that task in one sentence what is quicker to you it's a vital part of what we now do day-to-day</p>"
    },
